# What a rule decides, read by tests/functional_core.rs: no source of src/shell/ names one of these
# on a rule module, since the rule's outcome carries what it returns
# (ADR-0024). One name per line. A rule's own functions behind its
# outcome, as `undecided_lines` of docs/prose-width and `pending` of traceability/coverage, are
# private, so the compiler holds them; for `nuc explain` the shell asks `config::explanation`,
# which returns a rule's ID and reason only, so no check reaches the shell through it.

# A rule as a whole, whose check the shell would call by name.
RULE
